  "label": "Cynical View of Consumption",
  "description": "The meme conveys a cynical perspective on consumption, suggesting that desirable things (like steak) are obtained through destruction or violence. This requires the viewer to understand the broader cultural and philosophical context of consumerism and the often-hidden costs of production. It critiques the disconnect between the consumer and the source of their food.",
